      "body": [
        {
          "type": "TextualBody",
          "label": "recto, left, Col. II",
          "value": "\n<ol><li>Also dis[p]ensed for them</li>\n<li>on Friday the 28th of that (month)</li>\n<li>five qin\u1e6d\u0101rs, numbering f(ive hundred) and 55 (loaves)</li>\n<li>\u1e62\u0101li\u1e25 4 Shema\u02bfya 5</li>\n<li>the silk worker 6 Ab\u016b Mukht\u0101r 7</li>\n<li>the orphans of the astrologer 8 the man from the \u1e24ij\u0101z 3</li>\n<li>Shemarya 4 al-\u02bfAmm\u0101ni 3</li>\n<li>the son of the deaf man 6 the mother-in-law of Eliyyahu and an orphan 2</li>\n<li>Za\u02bffar\u0101n 8 al-[&hellip;] 3</li>\n<li>Sab\u012b\u02bf and a blind man 5 Si[tt]\u0101n 3</li>\n<li>Umm Ibrahim 3 [the wife of] Avraham 2</li>\n<li>b. al-Kharaz\u012b (the son of the maker of beads) 2 the [w]ife of B[\u016b] Sa\u02bf\u012bd 6</li>\n<li>a semi-paralyzed woman 2 Khal\u012bf the blind man 4</li>\n<li>Umm Hil\u0101la 2 Yi\u1e63\u1e25aq and his in-law 6</li>\n<li>the in-law of R. Yosef 8<del> all </del>Yehuda 3</li>\n<li>the acquaintance of the dyer 3 the man from Mal\u012bj 6</li>\n<li>Umm Khal\u012bf 3 the mother-in-law of the son of the woman from Palestine 3</li>\n<li>the female washer of the dead for the R\u016bm 2 the cantor and his in-law 6</li>\n<li>the mother-in-law of the parnas of the R\u016bm 8 Eliyyahu 2</li>\n<li>the mother-in-law of al-Mu\u1e6d\u0101lib\u012b 2 Sam\u012b\u1e25 the Kohen 4</li>\n<li>Wah\u012bb 3 the mother-in-law of the elder 2</li>\n<li>the man from Sicily 4 Sab\u012b\u02bf 4</li>\n<li>Eliakim 2 his brother [&hellip;]</li>\n<li>Aharon from Jerusalem 4 the Kohen and the brother of his mother and his grandmother 4</li>\n<li><del>his mother and grandmother 4</del> the orphans of Yosef 6</li>\n<li>Ra\u1e25amim 3 Umm al-Khayy\u0101\u1e6d (the mother of the tailor) 3 <del>2</del></li>\n<li>Natan 2 Ya\u02bfaqov [&hellip;]</li>\n<li>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; 86&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;91</li></ol>\n",
